{"name":"Tree Line","hex":"#c3db8d","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tree line","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A division in altitude (or latitude) above which trees tend not to grow on mountains."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tree_line"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tree line","blocks":[{"text":"The tree line is the edge of a habitat at which trees can grow and beyond which they cannot. It is found at high elevations and high latitudes. Beyond the tree line, trees cannot tolerate the environmental conditions. The tree line is sometimes distinguished from a lower timberline, which is the line below which trees form a forest with a closed canopy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Tree_line_above_St._Moritz.jpg/330px-Tree_line_above_St._Moritz.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_line","wikidata":"Q207762"},{"title":"Tree","blocks":[{"text":"In botany, a tree is a perennial plant with an elongated stem, or trunk, usually supporting branches and leaves. In some usages, the definition of a tree may be narrower, e.g., including only woody plants with secondary growth, only plants that are usable for timber, or only plants above a specified height. Wider definitions include taller palms, tree ferns, bananas, and bamboos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Usamljeni_jasen_-_panoramio_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree","wikidata":"Q10884"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Tree_line.jpg/500px-Tree_line.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Tree_line.jpg/500px-Tree_line.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"In this view of an alpine tree line, the distant line looks particularly sharp. The foreground shows the transition from trees to no trees. These trees are stunted in growth and one-sided because of cold and constant wind.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATree_line.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/de/Distribution_of_Plants_in_a_Perpendicular_Direction_in_the_Torrid%2C_the_Temperate%2C_and_the_Rigid_Zones_1848_Alexander_Keith_Johnston.png/500px-Distribution_of_Plants_in_a_Perpendicular_Direction_in_the_Torrid%2C_the_Temperate%2C_and_the_Rigid_Zones_1848_Alexander_Keith_Johnston.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/de/Distribution_of_Plants_in_a_Perpendicular_Direction_in_the_Torrid%2C_the_Temperate%2C_and_the_Rigid_Zones_1848_Alexander_Keith_Johnston.png/1280px-Distribution_of_Plants_in_a_Perpendicular_Direction_in_the_Torrid%2C_the_Temperate%2C_and_the_Rigid_Zones_1848_Alexander_Keith_Johnston.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/d/de/Distribution_of_Plants_in_a_Perpendicular_Direction_in_the_Torrid%2C_the_Temperate%2C_and_the_Rigid_Zones_1848_Alexander_Keith_Johnston.png/500px-Distribution_of_Plants_in_a_Perpendicular_Direction_in_the_Torrid%2C_the_Temperate%2C_and_the_Rigid_Zones_1848_Alexander_Keith_Johnston.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"This map of the \"Distribution of Plants in a Perpendicular Direction in the Torrid, the Temperate, and the Frigid Zones\" was first published 1848 in \"The Physical Atlas\". It shows tree lines of the Andes, Tenerife, Himalaya, Alps, Pyrenees, and Lapland.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADistribution_of_Plants_in_a_Perpendicular_Direction_in_the_Torrid%2C_the_Temperate%2C_and_the_Rigid_Zones_1848_Alexander_Keith_Johnston.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Bistrishko-Branishte.jpg/500px-Bistrishko-Branishte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Bistrishko-Branishte.jpg/500px-Bistrishko-Branishte.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Alpine tree line of mountain pine and European spruce below the subalpine zone of Bistrishko Branishte, with the surmounting Golyam Rezen Peak, Vitosha Mountain, Sofia, Bulgaria","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABistrishko-Branishte.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Treeline_In_The_Tararuas.JPG/500px-Treeline_In_The_Tararuas.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Treeline_In_The_Tararuas.JPG/1280px-Treeline_In_The_Tararuas.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Treeline_In_The_Tararuas.JPG/500px-Treeline_In_The_Tararuas.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An alpine tree line in the Tararua Range","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATreeline_In_The_Tararuas.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Rivi%C3%A8re_aux_M%C3%A9l%C3%A8zes_1.JPG/500px-Rivi%C3%A8re_aux_M%C3%A9l%C3%A8zes_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c0/Rivi%C3%A8re_aux_M%C3%A9l%C3%A8zes_1.JPG/500px-Rivi%C3%A8re_aux_M%C3%A9l%C3%A8zes_1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The tree line visible in the lower left, while trees also grow in the sheltered river valleys, northern Quebec, Ca